### 0. Health Check (Spring Boot Actuator)
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/health

### 1. Create a Product (Returns 201 Created)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "iPhone 17",
  "description": "Apple smartphone",
  "price": 79999.00,
  "active": true,
  "stock": 10
}

### 2. Get All Products (Paginated)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/products?page=0&size=10

### 3. Get Product by ID
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/products/1

### 4. Search and Filter Products (with pagination and sorting)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/products/search?search=iPhone&active=true&page=0&size=5&sortBy=price&direction=desc

### 5. Update a Product (with inventory stock update and fractional price)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/products/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "iPhone 17 Pro",
  "description": "Apple premium smartphone",
  "price": 99999.99,
  "active": true,
  "stock": 15
}

### 6. Delete a Product
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/v1/products/1

### 7. Purchase Product directly (legacy single purchase with @Retryable concurrency control)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/products/1/purchase
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 2
}

### 8. Create an Order (Returns 201 Created, with Customer identity & @Retryable)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerEmail": "alice@example.com",
  "customerName": "Alice Johnson",
  "shippingAddress": "456 Market St, San Francisco, CA",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": 1,
      "quantity": 2
    }
  ]
}

### 9. Get All Orders (Paginated)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders?page=0&size=10&direction=desc

### 10. Get Order by ID
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders/1

### 11. Cancel a Pending Order
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders/1/cancel

### 12. Confirm a Pending Order
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders/1/confirm